From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: acqxi <kacqxi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:17:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] WSL host bridge: helper, native link path and Desktop
 supervisor

WSL agents can hand work that needs Windows to the Windows backend on the
same computer through native Linked environments. The Desktop starts
`t3 __host-bridge` in the WSL distro with the WSL backend's own launch, and
the helper listens on WSL loopback only. Each connection rides the helper's
stdio to the Desktop, which connects it to its own Windows backend on Windows
loopback. Frames carry streams, never addresses.

A link made with `sameHostBridge` accepts only this machine's loopback, and
the pairing code goes only to an address that answers as the expected
environment ID. The refusal of loopback for a picked machine is unchanged.

The supervisor waits for both backends and backs off exponentially. It
restarts the helper after WSL restarts and after resume, and pauses when the
Windows environment ID differs from the one paired.

The app reports why pairing failed, and the Desktop keeps it as the
bridge's last error, also once the bridge is off.
